Assertions:
[STATE] PLUGIN_NAMES contains 'sales-rep' and PLUGINS_ERRORS is empty - the plugin list names the hub plugin without errors {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the left rail carries a 'Sales Rep hub' section holding 'Dashboard', 'My customers' and 'Tasks' {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL_DASH ends with /company/dashboard and WIDGETS_FIRST is at least 1 {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL_CUST ends with /company/my-customers {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL_PROFILE is {{FRONT_URL}}/company/my-customers/@td(ORG_ACME.platform_id) -- the route takes the organization platform id, not the business key {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL_ORDERS ends with /orders and contains @td(ORG_ACME.platform_id) {SPEC}
[SHAPE] ORDER_NO_SHOWN is not empty - the opened order renders its own number {SPEC}
[NAV] URL_ALL is {{FRONT_URL}}/company/customer-orders {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL_TASKS ends with /company/tasks {OBSERVED}
[REL] every URL in HUB_SCRIPTS other than host federation/routing runtime chunks (/assets/remoteEntry-*, /assets/*__mfe_internal__host__*, /assets/plugin-route-placeholder-*) is under /modules/$(VirtoCommerce.SalesRep)/plugins/vc-frontend/ - the host /assets/ folder serves no hub PAGE chunk {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] entries of PLUGIN_REQS whose status is not 200 or 304 == 0, and PLUGIN_REQS contains mf-manifest.json (content-type application/json) and remoteEntry.js {OBSERVED}
[REL] H1_DASH, H1_CUST, H1_PROFILE, H1_ORDERS, H1_ALL and H1_TASKS are non-empty and pairwise different, and none contains 'Page not found' - a route that fell to the host catch-all would repeat the Not Found text {SPEC}
[REL] WIDGETS_SECOND equals WIDGETS_FIRST - the dashboard is the same page the second time, not a re-registered duplicate or a half-mounted one {SPEC}
[COUNT] sections named 'Sales Rep hub' in the left rail == 1 on every hub screen of the journey (Dashboard, My customers, Customer profile, Customer orders, All customer orders, Tasks) -- the host order page reached from the order row (/account/orders/<id>) is a theme page and carries no hub rail, so it is excluded - a plugin that registers its rail section twice shows two {OBSERVED}
[STATE] H1_TASKS contains 'Tasks' {OBSERVED}

[REL] for each of the five routes FINAL_URL_n equals the URL that was requested - no redirect and no rewrite for a rep {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] frames containing the host Not Found text ('Page not found') across FRAMES_1..FRAMES_5 == 0 - the placeholder hands over to the real page without a Not Found flash {OBSERVED}
[SHAPE] each H1_n is non-empty and contains no dotted i18n key token {SPEC}
[REL] the five H1 values are pairwise different (a page that fell to a shared fallback would repeat) {SPEC}
[STATE] every T_n is at most 5 s (measured 1.07-1.64 s on vcst; 5 s is the stuck-spinner threshold of this suite) {OBSERVED}

[REL] for all six routes FINAL_URL_n equals {{FRONT_URL}}/account/dashboard - the guard sends a non-rep home from every hub route {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] frames containing the host Not Found text ('Page not found') across FRAMES_1..FRAMES_6 == 0 - no transient Not Found before the redirect {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] SR_GQL_REQS == 0 - no salesRep* operation is sent to /graphql/sales-rep for a non-rep, asserted at the network layer and not only by an absent link {BL}
[REL] every BACK_URL_n equals PREV_URL_n and none is a hub route (/company/dashboard|my-customers|customer-orders|tasks|documents) - the redirect replaced the history entry, so Back neither re-enters the hub route nor loops {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] sections named 'Sales Rep hub' in the left rail of the landing page == 0 {BL}

[STATE] ME_PERMS does not contain 'sales-rep:access' and ME_ADMIN is false - the guard precondition; a platform administrator would short-circuit every gate and make this case vacuous {BL}
[REL] FINAL_URL_1..FINAL_URL_4 each equal {{FRONT_URL}}/account/dashboard {BL}
[COUNT] BODY_1..BODY_4 containing 'Page not found' == 0 - the refusal is a redirect, not a dead end {SPEC}
[COUNT] SR_GQL_REQS == 0 - no operation reaches /graphql/sales-rep for this maintainer {BL}

[NAV] for each of /company/my-customers, /company/customer-orders, /company/tasks and /company/documents the final URL (URL_ANON_1..URL_ANON_4) has the path /sign-in and a returnUrl query value equal to the requested path {SPEC}
[NAV] URL_ANON path is /sign-in and its returnUrl query value is /company/dashboard {SPEC}
[NAV] URL_REP is {{FRONT_URL}}/company/dashboard and WIDGETS_REP is at least 1 - a rep is returned to the hub after signing in {SPEC}
[NAV] URL_BUYER is {{FRONT_URL}}/account/dashboard - a returnUrl that points at a hub route does not leak the hub to a non-rep {BL}
[COUNT] WIDGETS_BUYER == 0 {BL}

[COUNT] errors[] entries in PLUGINS_RESP == 0 - the plugin list is readable without a session {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] ERROR_TOASTS == 0 - an anonymous visitor is not shown an authorization error {SPEC}
[COUNT] sections named 'Sales Rep hub' plus links named 'Sales reps' in the page == 0 {BL}
[COUNT] SR_GQL_REQS == 0 {BL}

[COUNT] RAIL_REP == 0, LINK_REP == 0 and LINK_BUYER == 0 - neither the rail section nor the Corporate link renders while the setting is off {SPEC}
[COUNT] PLUGIN_REQS_REP == 0 and PLUGIN_REQS_BUYER == 0 - the when: gate is evaluated before any plugin code is fetched, so a disabled store ships no plugin bytes to its visitors {SPEC}
[STATE] URL_DASH and URL_SR each end on either /account/dashboard or the host 'Page not found' page, and neither BODY_DASH nor BODY_SR holds hub content (widgets, the Sales reps table) {SPEC}

[COUNT] occurrences of a dotted i18n key token (matches /sales_rep\.[a-z_.]+/i or /^[A-Z_]+\.[A-Z_.]+$/ or the literal PAGE.TITLE) in RAIL_TEXT_DE, RAIL_TEXT_ES, RAIL_TEXT_NOLOC, PAGE_TEXT_DE, PAGE_TEXT_ES, PAGE_TEXT_NOLOC and in CORP_DE, CORP_ES, CORP_NOLOC == 0 {BL}
[REL] RAIL_DE differs from RAIL_EN and CORP_DE differs from CORP_EN - German is translated, not English text under a German culture {OBSERVED}
[REL] RAIL_ES differs from RAIL_EN and CORP_ES differs from CORP_EN {SPEC}
[REL] RAIL_NOLOC equals RAIL_EN and CORP_NOLOC equals CORP_EN - a culture with no plugin locale file falls back to English, never to a raw key {OBSERVED}
[SHAPE] H1_DE, H1_ES and H1_NOLOC are non-empty {SPEC}

[COUNT] LINK_FRAMES entries matching a dotted i18n key token (matches /sales_rep\.[a-z_.]+/i or /^[A-Z_]+\.[A-Z_.]+$/ or the literal PAGE.TITLE) == 0 - the link never shows its raw title key {BL}
[REL] every non-empty LINK_FRAMES entry equals FINAL_LINK - no frame shows a label different from the settled one {BL}
[COUNT] PAGE_FRAMES entries (H1 or a column header) matching a dotted i18n key token (matches /sales_rep\.[a-z_.]+/i or /^[A-Z_]+\.[A-Z_.]+$/ or the literal PAGE.TITLE) == 0 {BL}

[COUNT] every RAIL_* == 0 and every LINK_* == 0 - an unusable manifest withdraws the rail section and the Corporate link, it never leaves a link to a dead route {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] every OVERLAY_* == 0 - no uncaught error overlay on any of the four home loads {BL}
[SHAPE] PDP_REP404 is non-empty - the storefront stays usable when the plugin cannot be delivered {BL}
[STATE] each of BODY_REP404, BODY_REPHTML, BODY_B404 and BODY_BHTML is not empty and either contains 'Page not found' or RELOAD_* is true - the visitor is never left on a blank page; the outcome is recorded: 3x on 2026-10-15 saw the host 'Page not found' page with no Reload page button in all four cases, and whether that is the intended state of a failed manifest is an open product question (VCST-6015 3x B2) {SPEC}
[CONSOLE] no uncaught exception (TypeError or ReferenceError); the single resource-error line for the faulted manifest request is expected {OBSERVED}

[COUNT] ENTRY_REQS == 0 - an incompatible plugin is rejected on its manifest alone, its entry script is never requested {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] RAIL == 0 and OVERLAY == 0 {OBSERVED}
[STATE] BODY_DASH is not empty and holds no hub content (no widgets, no hub table), and it either contains 'Page not found' or RELOAD_DASH is true - the visitor is never left on a blank page; the outcome is recorded, not pinned: 3x on 2026-10-15 saw the host 'Page not found' page with no Reload page button, and whether that is the intended state of a rejected plugin is an open product question (VCST-6015 3x B2) {SPEC}
[SHAPE] the home page rendered (its main navigation is present) although the plugin was rejected {SPEC}

[STATE] T_LOADER is at most 5 s - the visitor sees a loading indicator, not a blank page {OBSERVED}
[REL] T_LOADER is less than T_NOTICE, and T_NOTICE is at most 10 s - the slow-loading notice with a Reload page button appears while the entry is still pending (measured about 8.5 s; host README: about 7 s) {OBSERVED}
[REL] T_HUB is at least 15 s and FINAL_URL equals {{FRONT_URL}}/company/dashboard with WIDGETS at least 1 - the page recovers by itself once the entry arrives {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] FRAMES containing 'Page not found' == 0 {OBSERVED}

[COUNT] HUB_REP == 1 and HUB_DOCS == 1 - exactly one hub section for each rep, never a duplicate left over from the previous registration {SPEC}
[COUNT] HUB_BUYER == 0 - the buyer sees no hub section after a rep was signed in on the same tab {BL}
[COUNT] LINK_BUYER == 1 - the buyer sees exactly one Corporate Sales reps link {SPEC}
[REL] DOCS_REP == 0 and DOCS_DOCS >= 1 - the Document library entry follows the permission of the signed-in user, not of the first user of the tab {DOC}

[DOM] MESSAGE reads 'Part of the site could not be loaded. Please reload the page to continue.' {OBSERVED}
[STATE] RELOAD_BTN is true - the visitor is offered a way out {OBSERVED}
[REL] FINAL_URL equals {{FRONT_URL}}/company/dashboard and WIDGETS is at least 1 - Reload page recovers the hub without leaving the route {OBSERVED}
[COUNT] RAIL == 1 after the recovery - the failed first attempt left no half-registered duplicate {SPEC}

[COUNT] LABEL_FRAMES entries matching a dotted i18n key token (matches /sales_rep\.[a-z_.]+/i or /^[A-Z_]+\.[A-Z_.]+$/ or the literal PAGE.TITLE) == 0 - no frame at any moment shows a raw key in the rail, the page title, a widget heading or a table header {BL}
[REL] FIRST_RAIL equals FINAL_RAIL and FIRST_H1 equals FINAL_H1 - the label shown first is the label that stays {BL}
[SHAPE] FINAL_RAIL and FINAL_H1 are non-empty {SPEC}

[COUNT] LINKS_B_EN == 1, LINKS_B_DE == 1 and MOB_LINKS_B_DE == 1 - the buyer sees exactly one Corporate Sales reps link before and after the language switch, on desktop and in the 375px menu {SPEC}
[COUNT] HUB_R_EN == 1, HUB_R_DE == 1 and MOB_HUB_R_DE == 1 - the rep sees exactly one Sales Rep hub section before and after the switch, on desktop and in the 375px menu {SPEC}
[DOM] LABEL_B_DE and MOB_LABEL_B_DE read 'Vertriebsmitarbeiter' and HUB_LABEL_R_DE reads 'Vertriebsmitarbeiter-Hub' {OBSERVED}
[REL] LABEL_B_DE differs from LABEL_B_EN and HUB_LABEL_R_DE differs from HUB_LABEL_R_EN - the labels were translated by the switch, not left in English {SPEC}
[COUNT] occurrences of a dotted i18n key token (matches /sales_rep\.[a-z_.]+/i or /^[A-Z_]+\.[A-Z_.]+$/ or the literal PAGE.TITLE) in RAIL_TEXT_B_DE, MOB_TEXT_B_DE, RAIL_TEXT_R_DE and MOB_TEXT_R_DE == 0 {BL}
